<meta name=3D"viewport" content=3D"width=3Ddevice-width,initial-scale=3D1">
<title>Career Compass =E2=80=94 Ideal Job Explorer</title>

</head>
<body>
<div class=3D"shell">
<header><div class=3D"brand"><div class=3D"mark"></div><div><h1>Career Comp=
ass</h1><div class=3D"small">Ideal Job Explorer =C2=B7 Senior High School</=
div></div></div><div class=3D"tag">INDIVIDUAL PROJECT</div></header>

<section id=3D"intro" class=3D"card">
  <div class=3D"hero-grid">
    <div>
      <span class=3D"section-chip">START HERE</span>
      <h2>What kind of work could feel right for you?</h2>
      <p class=3D"lead">Explore two things: <b>what naturally interests you=
</b> and <b>what you want your work to stand for</b>. Your result is a care=
er hypothesis =E2=80=94 not a label and not a final decision.</p>
      <p class=3D"small">There are 42 quick statements. Rate each from 1 (n=
ot like me) to 5 (very much like me). Answer honestly, not according to wha=
t you think sounds impressive.</p>
      <div class=3D"actions"><button id=3D"startBtn">Start the quiz</button=
></div>
    </div>
    <div class=3D"hero-art" aria-hidden=3D"true"><div class=3D"circle"></di=
v><div class=3D"sq"></div><div class=3D"line"></div></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id=3D"quiz" class=3D"card hidden">
  <div class=3D"progress-wrap">
    <div class=3D"progress-label"><span id=3D"progressText">Question 1 of 4=
2</span><span id=3D"pctText">0%</span></div>
    <div class=3D"bar"><div id=3D"progressBar"></div></div>
  </div>
  <span id=3D"sectionChip" class=3D"section-chip">INTERESTS</span>
  <div id=3D"questionText" class=3D"question"></div>
  <div class=3D"scale" id=3D"scale"></div>
  <div class=3D"nav no-print"><button class=3D"secondary" id=3D"backBtn">=
=E2=86=90 Back</button><button id=3D"nextBtn">Next =E2=86=92</button></div>
</section>

<section id=3D"results" class=3D"card hidden">
  <span class=3D"section-chip">YOUR CAREER COMPASS</span>
  <h2>Your results</h2>
  <p class=3D"lead" id=3D"summaryLine"></p>
  <div class=3D"result-grid">
    <div class=3D"result-box"><h3>1. Interest worlds</h3><div id=3D"interes=
tScores"></div></div>
    <div class=3D"result-box"><h3>2. Work values / calling</h3><div id=3D"v=
alueScores"></div></div>
  </div>
  <div class=3D"result-box" style=3D"margin-top:22px">
    <h3>3. Your strongest combination</h3>
    <div id=3D"badges"></div>
    <p id=3D"comboText" style=3D"line-height:1.6"></p>
    <div class=3D"prompt"><b>Your career question:</b><br><span id=3D"caree=
rQuestion"></span></div>
  </div>
  <div class=3D"result-box" style=3D"margin-top:22px">
    <h3>4. Job families worth exploring</h3>
    <p class=3D"small">These are starting points, not prescriptions. Circle=
 or copy the three that make you most curious.</p>
    <div id=3D"jobs" class=3D"jobs"></div>
  </div>
  <div class=3D"result-box" style=3D"margin-top:22px">
    <h3>5. Your next step</h3>
    <p>Use the writing worksheet to test your results against real evidence=
: subjects you enjoy, activities you choose voluntarily, strengths other pe=
ople notice, work conditions you value, and actual career research.</p>
  </div>
  <div class=3D"actions no-print"><button>Print / Save results</button><but=
ton class=3D"secondary" id=3D"restartBtn">Restart</button></div>
  <div class=3D"footer">This classroom explorer is inspired by widely used =
interest-and-work-value approaches. It is designed for reflection and discu=
ssion, not for psychological diagnosis or high-stakes career selection.<br>=
<br>Evangelia Domvrou / Teacher of English Language and Literature</div>
</section>
</div>



</body></html>
